+/*
+ * The register file: TCG's registers (indices 0-23 above) and BLOCK_PTR are
+ * i64 variables of the TB's function, accessed with tcg_out_op_global_*().
+ *
+ * On WASI they are locals, from local index REG_LOCAL_BASE on (see
+ * wasm_finalize_module).  A TB there always runs from its start to an exit:
+ * a helper returns or throws (cpu_loop_exit), and either way the TB is not
+ * re-entered half way.  So nothing must survive between calls of the
+ * function, and the host compiler can keep locals in machine registers,
+ * whereas every access to a global goes to memory.  (With Emscripten's
+ * coroutines, a helper can unwind out of the TB to re-enter it later at
+ * BLOCK_PTR, so there the registers must be globals.)
+ */
+#ifdef WASI_PLATFORM
+#define REG_LOCAL_BASE 8
+#endif
